## Repository Structure
The project lives in a single GitHub repository named good-night-games. Both the frontend and backend are subdirectories within it. This keeps all Good Night Games code in one place, allows shared TypeScript types between frontend and backend, and means one CI pipeline covers both sides.
```
good-night-games/                  ← GitHub repo root
├── frontend/                      ← Next.js app
├── backend/                       ← Hono API server
├── shared/                        ← TypeScript types shared by both sides (optional, add when needed)
├── .github/
│   └── workflows/
│       └── ci.yml                 ← single CI file covering frontend and backend
└── README.md
```
Each subdirectory has its own package.json and dependencies installed independently. There is no root-level package.json — run npm install inside frontend/ or backend/ as needed. Railway is configured with its Root Directory set to backend/ so it treats that folder as if it were a standalone repo.

